WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.460
I’m announcing my candidacy

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:02.180
for president

00:00:02.189 --> 00:00:03.820
for president of the United States

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:07.670
for president of the Unites States of America

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:09.500
Lots of people want to be president

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:12.200
It’s going to be so much easier the second time

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.700
I’m repulsed by lots of politicians.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.940
They pander to get our attention.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:18.160
To the new moon squad

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:18.720
Alright

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:20.760
Mayor Pete! To the road ahead

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:23.340
She’s 20, I’m 52 this is not fair!

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:24.800
[laughing]

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:27.640
A former prosecutor laughs with radio hosts

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:30.789
while lying about the music she liked in college.

00:00:30.789 --> 00:00:35.780
Oh my goodness oh yea definitely Snoop, Tupac.

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:36.840
But Snoop and Tupac

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:38.880
didn’t even perform when she was in college.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:40.230
And when they did,

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:43.489
she was busy imprisoning people on pot charges.

00:00:43.489 --> 00:00:46.460
Abraham Lincoln complained that politicians

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:49.719
are driven by a “voracious desire for office.”

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:52.020
Well it’s not better today.

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:56.180
Not only are they mad for power, they push bad ideas.

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:59.660
So here are some of this current candidates’ worst:

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:01.480
[mail truck sounds]

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:03.980
Are you ready for the Post Office to go into banking?

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:05.729
Bernie Sanders claims the

00:01:05.729 --> 00:01:07.980
Postal Service could make billions of dollars a year

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:11.079
by establishing basic banking services.

00:01:11.079 --> 00:01:13.689
Really? The people who mishandle mail?

00:01:13.689 --> 00:01:15.579
Oh my God are you kidding me?

00:01:15.579 --> 00:01:18.160
The Post Office just lost another billion dollars.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:19.840
Now they’re going to manage our money?

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:21.529
Sanders also wants

00:01:21.529 --> 00:01:25.420
A ban on for profit charter schools

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:27.279
Why? Sanders says

00:01:27.279 --> 00:01:29.180
I believe we do have a moral obligation

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:30.869
to lift up the poorest people

00:01:30.869 --> 00:01:32.460
But Sanders would freeze funding

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:34.620
for even non-profit charters,

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:36.660
like this one that helps kids succeed

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:38.660
after government schools failed.

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:42.540
Reading is work, but it’s rocking awesome!

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:44.880
Sanders should listen to his colleague Cory Booker.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:46.320
When people tell me they're against

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:48.360
school choice or charter schools,

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.560
I look at them and say as soon as you're telling me

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:54.580
you're willing to send your kid to a failing school

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:56.720
in my city then I'll be with you.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:59.780
Sensible, but unfortunately, that was years ago.

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:02.340
Now that Booker is a Democratic candidate,

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.559
he’s quiet about school choice.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:07.480
Instead, he wants the government to guarantee

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:10.880
everyone a job and to pay many people’s rent.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:13.560
We're going to have a very aggressive renter’s credit

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:15.420
The bad ideas keep coming.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:17.600
Senator Gillibrand wants to force everyone

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:20.480
to buy fertility treatment insurance.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:23.159
Real, structural change

00:02:23.159 --> 00:02:26.040
Elizabeth Warren plans to change all kinds of things

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:30.200
the cancellation of student loan debt of up to $50,000

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:34.060
She’d also ban all oil and gas drilling on federal land

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:36.930
Our very existence is at stake

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:38.880
Closing that pay gap.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:39.549
[APPLAUSE]

00:02:39.549 --> 00:02:41.680
Kamala Harris wants companies to

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:44.050
prove they pay men and women equally.

00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:46.520
There will be penalties if they don't.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:48.219
[APPLAUSE]

00:02:48.219 --> 00:02:50.540
But salaries vary for lots of reasons

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:52.680
unrelated to sexism.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:55.599
President Harris would also censor the internet.

00:02:55.599 --> 00:02:59.180
We will hold social media platforms accountable

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:02.700
for the hate infiltrating their platforms.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:03.720
That sounds nice,

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:06.700
but if politicians get to decide what is “hate,”

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:09.299
they’ll censor any idea they don’t like.

00:03:09.299 --> 00:03:12.760
The 1st Amendment is one of the defining features

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:13.920
of who we are

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.820
Good for Joe Biden for saying that,

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:18.130
but he’s got bad ideas, too.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:20.249
College should be free.

00:03:20.249 --> 00:03:23.480
Free? Colleges already jacked up tuition much

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:26.430
faster than the rate of inflation because

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:29.440
taxpayers subsidize too much of college.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:31.060
China! China! China!

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:34.080
The Republican front-runner has bad ideas too.

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:36.960
Our trade deficit in goods with the world

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:41.969
last year was nearly $800 billion dollars

00:03:41.969 --> 00:03:46.400
We lost on just trade 800 billion dollars

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:49.980
No Mr. President! We didn’t lose $800 billion.

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:52.670
The “trade deficit” just means foreigners

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:57.390
sent us $800 billion more goods than we sent them.

00:03:57.390 --> 00:04:01.400
We got products. In return, they got this paper,

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:03.700
which they’ll invest in the US.

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:06.719
So that’s good for us. It’s not a problem.

00:04:06.719 --> 00:04:08.340
No it’s crazy what they’re saying,

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:09.170
so many different things

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:12.510
Fortunately, the incumbent has some good ideas too.

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:18.080
We eliminated 30,000 pages of job killing regulations

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:19.590
from the Federal Register.

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:21.600
Now the president says he wants to shrink

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.780
the code to its 1960 size.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:24.840
This shows how

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:27.139
many rules we’re burdened by now.

00:04:27.139 --> 00:04:29.340
Some Democrats also say sensible things.

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:32.470
Mayor Pete Buttigieg criticizes his opponents

00:04:32.470 --> 00:04:34.650
for their “college for all” freebie.

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:37.160
I have a hard time getting my head around

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:40.340
the idea that a majority who earn less because

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:42.320
they didn't go to college would subsidize

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:44.460
a minority who earn more

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:46.260
And all the candidates could learn from

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:47.760
congresswoman Tulsi Gabbard.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:50.000
She served in Iraq and says

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.130
she knows the cost of war.

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:54.480
I will end the regime change wars.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:56.650
Taking the money that we’ve been wasting on these

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:58.380
wars and weapons and investing it

00:04:58.380 --> 00:04:59.979
and serving the needs of our people.

00:04:59.979 --> 00:05:02.060
But sadly, she wouldn’t give the money back

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:02.740
to the people.

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:04.650
She wants to spend it on other

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:06.780
big-government programs.

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:08.400
All the candidates have bad ideas,

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:10.120
but some are worse than others.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:12.800
Let us know in the comments below

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:16.340
who you think has the best and worst ideas.

